BotClient (experimental bot-token login)

Ported from VencordDBCPlugin (revision 6b2ee93a749b9a2c32d9fbc80d75dcf52e1cd48f)
https://github.com/aiko-chan-ai/VencordDBCPlugin
and the DiscordBotClient application it was built for
https://github.com/aiko-chan-ai/DiscordBotClient

Original authors: Elysia (aiko-chan-ai) and contributors.
License: GPL-3.0 (see LICENSE in this folder), same as Discord+ / Vencord.

Changes made for Discord+:
- Dexie storage replaced by @api/DataStore.
- window.BotClientNative / window.protoAPI (Electron preload bridges) replaced by renderer code:
  bot info is fetched with "Authorization: Bot <token>", settings protos live in DataStore.
- The ~134 user-only REST routes served by DiscordBotClient's local Express server are
  answered in the renderer (utils/restStubs.ts); only the routes needed so far are ported.
- Electron-shell only patches (custom title bar, tray, flashFrame) and the separate-window
  message editor were removed; only the legacy Embed Editor remains.
- Every behaviour change is gated by "bot mode", which is switched on only when a token is
  submitted in the plugin's login box, so regular user sessions are not touched.
